# The reviewer /ship runs for step 7, the security pass. Two shapes: agent:<name>
# dispatches that agent on this host, and anything else is a command line the
# audit prompt is appended to.
#
# `auto` means the shape is chosen when the gate runs: the security-reviewer
# agent when you have defined one in your own Claude agents directory, otherwise
# Claude Code with Fable in plan mode. With neither one there the gate stops and
# names this file rather than running nothing.
#
# Only your own directory is read, never the project being reviewed. A branch
# that could put an agent definition in the probe's path would be appointing the
# reviewer that audits it.
#
# For the same reason the gate refuses an agent: value, stated or chosen, when
# the repository being reviewed defines an agent of that name. The gate cannot
# tell which of the two definitions it would dispatch, so it stops and says so.
# Remove that file from the worktree, or name a command line here.
#
# So an agent that arrives through a plugin is invisible to the probe, and so is
# one a project defines for itself. On such a host write agent:security-reviewer
# here; an explicit value is never probed. An explicit agent: value on a host
# that cannot dispatch agents still stops the gate rather than running something
# else.
#
# Copy this file to config/security-reviewer to change it: /ship reads config/
# first and falls back here.
auto
